2
00:01:50,819 --> 00:01:53,196
I never had sex with a farm animal

3
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,490
or abused a girlfriend,

4
00:01:55,574 --> 00:01:58,702
unless you count marrying her.

5
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:01,913
Let me say, it was tough, uh...

6
00:02:01,997 --> 00:02:04,541
narrowing down my ten
most significant cases.

7
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:07,419
I prefer the smaller questions.

8
00:02:07,628 --> 00:02:12,007
Of my professional
memberships, my teaching.

9
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:14,801
Madam President, just
between you and me,

10
00:02:14,885 --> 00:02:18,680
my feeling is that it's not as
far-fetched as some people say.

11
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:22,934
I still think there is a universe

12
00:02:23,018 --> 00:02:25,687
where the ERA gets passed.

13
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:30,067
Women truly are the best, aren't they?

14
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:39,326
I am deeply honored to be considered
for the late Justice's seat.

15
00:02:41,203 --> 00:02:42,329
So, tell me.

16
00:02:45,749 --> 00:02:48,168
How did they buy you? The Shepherds.

17
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:50,605
Judge Abruzzo, Madam President,
I hate to break this up.

18
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:54,633
Oh, I have already taken too much
of the president's valuable time.

19
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:56,343
Madam President.

20
00:02:57,844 --> 00:02:59,204
- Mr. Vice President.
- Your Honor.

21
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:01,765
It has been a sincere pleasure.

22
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:08,772
I'll set up Judge Michaels for
the end of the day tomorrow?

23
00:03:12,192 --> 00:03:14,152
I have Secretary Durant waiting for you.

24
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:18,532
I felt emasculated.

25
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:20,574
Excuse me.

26
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:24,788
Bill Shepherd guiding my hand.

27
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:27,708
And you looked emasculated, Mark.

28
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:32,963
- You're mistaken.
- No, I'm not mistaken.

29
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:34,607
- I watched your face.
- Madam President...

30
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:36,466
Please don't call me that. Please.

31
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:38,093
- Claire.
- Better.

32
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:41,638
- Claire.
- Yes. What?

33
00:03:41,722 --> 00:03:43,322
That was not a fight you were gonna win.

34
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:45,308
- Do you like being the messenger?
- What?

35
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:47,811
Has it been a dream of some sort
since you were a little boy?

36
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:49,354
Because I can tell you something.

37
00:03:49,438 --> 00:03:53,024
Once you identify the degree
to which you are boxed in,

38
00:03:53,108 --> 00:03:54,818
you'll see how liberating it is.

39
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:56,361
Are you with me...

40
00:03:56,695 --> 00:03:58,697
or are you with those
horrible, horrible people

41
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,157
you've attached yourself to?

42
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,951
Because I can tell you
something about Bill Shepherd.

43
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:04,453
I could smell it on him.

44
00:04:04,536 --> 00:04:07,831
The way I could on my
father, on my mother.

45
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:09,791
He's sick.

46
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:12,002
- Well, he was.
- He is.

47
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:15,297
And then where will that leave you?

48
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:16,570
With her?

49
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:17,924
Annette Shepherd?

50
00:04:18,008 --> 00:04:19,676
I know what that woman is,

51
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:22,846
and more to the point, isn't capable of.

52
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:27,267
And that little encounter with
the honorable Judge Abruzzo

53
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,895
at the fundraiser, that was
orchestrated too, wasn't it?

54
00:04:29,978 --> 00:04:30,978
Yes.

55
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:37,194
I look at him sometimes and
imagine him at six years old.

56
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:40,155
Was he always so deliberative?

57
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,281
Cautious?

58
00:04:42,866 --> 00:04:44,451
And I think in another life...

59
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:46,828
some other context

60
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:48,663
might we have been friends.

61
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,877
It's time to decide, Mark.

62
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:57,547
I hold every president
to the same standard.

63
00:04:57,631 --> 00:05:00,050
Are you making America better,

64
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:03,386
or are you making America worse?

65
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:04,971
That's all that matters...

66
00:05:05,055 --> 00:05:06,908
Excuse me. Could you
turn this off, please?

67
00:05:06,932 --> 00:05:09,810
- Yes, sir.
- The level of discourse in this city.

68
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:13,313
I'm telling you. She does have a point.

69
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:17,234
You need to tell Duncan to be careful
when it comes to his pit bull.

70
00:05:20,195 --> 00:05:21,195
City.

71
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:24,741
FDR turned this place into a city.

72
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:28,787
With his agencies and armies of clerks.

73
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:30,747
All the professors that followed.

74
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:33,750
Before the war, this was
just a small Southern town.

75
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:36,837
One built of marble, yeah, but just a...

76
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:39,548
small town sitting on a swamp.

77
00:05:40,215 --> 00:05:41,341
Place to visit.

78
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:43,634
Place to...

79
00:05:43,969 --> 00:05:45,470
protect the Republic.

80
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:49,224
Secure States' rights.

81
00:05:50,308 --> 00:05:51,935
That's not what it is today.

82
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:54,879
Some top-down money
grab for bureaucrats,

83
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:57,200
lobbyists and the entire
Democratic party.

84
00:05:57,274 --> 00:06:00,819
- You've always been more Teddy.
- Than that traitor pig Franklin?

85
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:05,156
Look, I know it's a sacrifice for
you to be here, in Washington.

86
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:08,285
But for God's sake, why take
the same room he was in?

87
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:09,660
Well...

88
00:06:09,703 --> 00:06:11,705
Well, he wanted to keep an eye on her.

89
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:15,959
Francis never could let
go of the White House.

90
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:19,462
But he did give us the opportunity
we've been waiting for.

91
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:21,756
She's not qualified.

92
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:24,384
She stole the damn thing.

93
00:06:25,135 --> 00:06:28,597
If ever there was ever a chance to
shrink the office down to size,

94
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,057
it's the presidency of Claire Underwood.

95
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:33,935
Maybe you should run for office.

96
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:36,354
I think that time has passed.

97
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:40,859
I'm worried about you.

98
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:43,320
Oh, don't be.

99
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:45,864
Never better.

100
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:52,704
Deregulation bill is the
first of a hundred,

101
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:54,623
ready and waiting.

102
00:06:54,706 --> 00:06:57,334
The speed you're moving at...

103
00:07:01,463 --> 00:07:04,299
I can come back. The lawyers
are due any minute.

104
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:07,385
No, no. Come on in here. Grab
yourself a cup of something.

105
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:10,180
I know Annette wanted to
talk to you in person,

106
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:11,848
before the rest of the team arrives.

107
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:14,392
I passed on what you told
me about the president.

108
00:07:14,476 --> 00:07:15,756
I want you to have it all before

109
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,437
Duncan got his hands on it.

110
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,940
She admitted to all
three of the abortions.

111
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:23,234
But I can get you the names
of the men. Who they were.

112
00:07:24,027 --> 00:07:26,446
No, I'm not comfortable with this.

113
00:07:26,947 --> 00:07:28,823
Let's take that off the table for now.

114
00:07:28,907 --> 00:07:30,116
She'll play along.

115
00:07:30,617 --> 00:07:31,868
We'll make sure of it.

116
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:44,172
I always imagined that
if I were president,

117
00:07:44,255 --> 00:07:46,800
I would want you to be a
member of my cabinet.

118
00:07:48,927 --> 00:07:50,303
You look like a movie star.

119
00:07:50,387 --> 00:07:54,265
Oh, well, it's the glare. I
get migraines since the fall.

120
00:07:54,349 --> 00:07:57,394
- They can come on quite suddenly.
- Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.

121
00:07:58,812 --> 00:08:01,940
The vice president said that you
wanted to meet me in person.

122
00:08:03,942 --> 00:08:05,568
It's so good to see you.

123
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:07,361
Sit.

124
00:08:11,825 --> 00:08:15,161
Not everyone comes back from
a fall like that, Cathy.

125
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:16,329
Yes.

126
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:19,165
I'm starting to feel
like a proverbial cat.

127
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:23,211
Take off your glasses,
let me see your eyes.

128
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:33,179
You have no shortage of stories.

129
00:08:33,263 --> 00:08:34,389
You know that.

130
00:08:35,015 --> 00:08:37,642
My memory's been very erratic lately.

131
00:08:37,726 --> 00:08:40,061
Sometimes, I think I might just forget

132
00:08:40,145 --> 00:08:44,190
the details of my time in
office altogether if...

133
00:08:45,275 --> 00:08:46,359
If?

134
00:08:48,770 --> 00:08:50,939
Honestly, I would love nothing more

135
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:54,280
than to just move on, Madam President.

136
00:08:54,576 --> 00:08:57,078
Well, I understand that
you have a job offer.

137
00:08:57,454 --> 00:08:59,330
Several. I'm lucky.

138
00:08:59,414 --> 00:09:02,459
The Eisenhower Strategic
Initiative, isn't it?

139
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:05,378
Yes, a think tank makes sense.
Outside of government.

140
00:09:05,462 --> 00:09:07,130
Well, not entirely outside.

141
00:09:07,464 --> 00:09:08,715
And heavily funded by...

142
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:12,552
A coalition of industrialists
and civic-minded folk, yes.

143
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:14,846
Big plans to change the world.

144
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:16,180
Hmm.

145
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,350
I haven't accepted.

146
00:09:19,434 --> 00:09:20,685
But you want to.

147
00:09:22,771 --> 00:09:24,647
You think I shouldn't take the job?

148
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:27,692
I think you should
trust your gut, Cathy.

149
00:09:29,611 --> 00:09:30,820
Take care of yourself.

150
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:35,700
Claire.

151
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:41,164
I'm sorry I didn't
write after Francis...

152
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:43,083
Oh, there's no need to apologize.

153
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:48,004
I can still feel his hand...

154
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,298
on my back.

155
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:54,052
Cathy, he's gone.

156
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:00,850
Bill Shepherd got to her.

157
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:03,603
I can feel it. She's going to testify.

158
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:06,314
My lawyers tell me her
team is still negotiating,

159
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:07,899
maybe for a while yet.

160
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:10,235
She thinks she's safe
with them, with this job.

161
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:12,195
Instead they're gonna
be sentencing her to...

162
00:10:17,951 --> 00:10:20,411
It needs to look like
complications from her fall.

163
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:24,040
I can have her detail pulled.
I still know some people.

164
00:10:24,415 --> 00:10:26,417
The opportunity will present itself.

165
00:10:29,754 --> 00:10:32,674
One last piece connecting
us both to Francis.

166
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:38,847
The world is either with
us or against us, Doug.

167
00:10:51,526 --> 00:10:53,278
You think you'll ever wear them?

168
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,323
Doesn't feel right.

169
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:59,200
Do you know the last
thing he said to me?

170
00:10:59,868 --> 00:11:01,828
"Promise me you and Doug

171
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:04,122
will take care of each other."

172
00:11:10,210 --> 00:11:12,379
I want to thank the National Gallery

173
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,960
for curating this magnificent exhibit.

174
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:17,886
Our hope is, in due time,

175
00:11:17,969 --> 00:11:21,139
these works of art will return
to their rightful place

176
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:25,351
in Afghanistan, Iraq and Syria.

177
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:31,024
Mr. Nasser.

178
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:33,818
They're making a fool of
you, these Shepherds.

179
00:11:33,902 --> 00:11:35,653
The special interests. The go-betweens.

180
00:11:35,737 --> 00:11:39,490
Your so-called peacekeeping in
Syria was a shameless land grab

181
00:11:39,574 --> 00:11:42,327
built on the lives of American
soldiers you sent into battle.

182
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:46,331
Then you can blame
Jane Davis, Mr. Nasser.

183
00:11:46,414 --> 00:11:47,414
I do.

184
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:49,959
I had hoped to renegotiate the deal

185
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,960
Jane helped broker many months ago.

186
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:54,756
Now I know that's impossible.

187
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:57,425
Oh, because she's
conveniently unavailable.

188
00:11:57,508 --> 00:11:59,928
Because you're in no position to do so.

189
00:12:00,011 --> 00:12:01,930
You've been excluded, just as I have.

190
00:12:02,013 --> 00:12:03,806
They're stripping power from you.

191
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:06,517
Have you ever seen the
Baathist playbook?

192
00:12:07,101 --> 00:12:10,146
It was inspired by American
intelligence agencies.

193
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:13,233
Sometimes, you need to be an
insurgent in your own country.

194
00:12:13,316 --> 00:12:15,036
Well, that's interesting.
Because presently,

195
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:18,071
I'm meeting with a member of a
known terrorist organization.

196
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:20,949
Pardon me. But I'm a lawyer.

197
00:12:21,030 --> 00:12:22,799
If you allow American
corporate interests

198
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,243
to cut ICO out of Syria's future...

199
00:12:24,244 --> 00:12:26,829
Are you about to
threaten me, Mr. Nasser?

200
00:12:26,913 --> 00:12:30,124
No, but we all know
what ICO is capable of.

201
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:32,669
I'm merely conveying a message
from one of my clients.

202
00:12:33,044 --> 00:12:36,547
You and your client
are one and the same.

203
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:41,119
Americans have such
faith in their ability

204
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:43,000
to keep things and people safe.

205
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:50,270
Mr. Nasser, Syria is a country of...

206
00:12:50,979 --> 00:12:54,816
former schools, former homes,
former places of worship.

207
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:58,278
Your organization played a
large part in the destruction.

208
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,822
And so have you, Madam President.

209
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:03,741
I'm afraid I can't help you.

210
00:13:04,826 --> 00:13:05,826
No...

211
00:13:07,245 --> 00:13:08,371
you can't.

212
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:19,799
I got two daughters, a beautiful wife.

213
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:21,884
Paid my dues.

214
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:23,511
Four terms.

215
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:27,765
A Republican in a diverse district.

216
00:13:29,434 --> 00:13:31,561
I got a ground operation second to none.

217
00:13:31,811 --> 00:13:33,021
And my volunteers,

218
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:34,279
their sons and their daughters are

219
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,560
coming up right behind 'em. I just...

220
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,443
I just feel like, um...

221
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:41,971
this could be my moment, you know?

222
00:13:43,031 --> 00:13:45,312
Fred told me about the legislation
about to be introduced.

223
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:46,366
Mm-hmm.

224
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,120
I'm co-signing.

225
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,331
- It's...
- Ambitious.

226
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:54,000
It's unprecedented.

227
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:56,252
It's bipartisan, is what it is.

228
00:13:56,753 --> 00:13:57,837
You worked for her.

229
00:13:58,921 --> 00:14:00,423
I worked for her husband.

230
00:14:01,341 --> 00:14:03,760
Nobody wants her hands
on a nuclear football.

231
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:06,929
Or sending any more uniforms
anywhere, here or abroad.

232
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:10,099
You're gonna have to be okay with that.

233
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:11,516
Are you?

234
00:14:13,436 --> 00:14:14,729
I owe her nothing.

235
00:14:19,108 --> 00:14:20,228
So what do they have on you?

236
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:25,073
Hold on, slugger.

237
00:14:26,824 --> 00:14:28,424
I'm still trying to get acquainted here.

238
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:33,581
- Right.
- Where do you think you're going?

239
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:35,750
Fred Amburg asked me to meet you.

240
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:38,252
- Well, Fred asked me to meet you.
- And we've met.

241
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,090
Where do you get off?

242
00:14:42,924 --> 00:14:45,843
- After where you've been.
- You mean where I was.

243
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,512
With Mr. Amburg.

244
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:49,180
The last person you worked for...

245
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:51,682
Became the President
of the United States.

246
00:14:51,766 --> 00:14:54,102
He pushed you out.

247
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:58,314
I am your chance.

248
00:15:00,691 --> 00:15:03,111
You know, not that I have
to prove myself to you,

249
00:15:03,194 --> 00:15:04,362
or to anyone else,

250
00:15:05,196 --> 00:15:06,906
but I can find the opening,

251
00:15:08,491 --> 00:15:10,701
the crack, the weak spot.

252
00:15:11,494 --> 00:15:12,537
I don't know,

253
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:15,623
maybe it's a curse to
know what people fear.

254
00:15:17,125 --> 00:15:18,209
Like you.

255
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:21,087
I think what scares you, Congressman.

256
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:22,880
Your base,

257
00:15:22,964 --> 00:15:25,049
your ground game, all that love.

258
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:27,051
You thought you deserved it,

259
00:15:27,677 --> 00:15:30,054
that it was meant for
you and nobody else.

260
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:31,930
You got blind.

261
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:35,143
You forgot that they'd come for you.

262
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:37,687
But they will come.

263
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:40,231
That's how this business is built.

264
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,735
So, I'm going to ask you again.

265
00:15:46,154 --> 00:15:48,114
What is it that they have on you?

266
00:15:53,911 --> 00:15:56,581
My district covers O'Hare.

267
00:15:58,624 --> 00:15:59,624
Pensions.

268
00:16:00,543 --> 00:16:02,962
The baggage handlers. I...

269
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:08,134
Shit.

270
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:13,848
It was stupid.

271
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:15,599
Well...

272
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,686
it's only stupid if you
can't make it go away.

273
00:16:24,692 --> 00:16:26,277
Tom, calm down.

274
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,446
I'm getting too old to be polite.

275
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:31,032
Hear the deal out. Content
will not be changed.

276
00:16:31,115 --> 00:16:33,326
And you and I both know better.

277
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:37,830
Something happened that night.

278
00:16:37,914 --> 00:16:39,540
Their marriage was broken,

279
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:40,958
he went over there.

280
00:16:41,042 --> 00:16:42,627
I'm not saying they're connected,

281
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:45,004
but the next day he winds up dead.

282
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:46,839
She knew an indictment was coming.

283
00:16:46,923 --> 00:16:49,550
Do you understand what that means?

284
00:16:49,634 --> 00:16:50,635
Then keep writing.

285
00:16:50,718 --> 00:16:54,055
So they can turn it into a 140
characters for clickbait?

286
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:56,098
We don't write anymore,

287
00:16:56,182 --> 00:16:57,975
we come up with feed for the trough.

288
00:16:58,059 --> 00:17:00,770
Put that goddamn thing
down before I smash it!

289
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:02,980
You need to go back in there

290
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:04,482
and apologize.

291
00:17:04,941 --> 00:17:07,401
To whom, Dayna?

292
00:17:08,069 --> 00:17:12,198
Our new boss is a voice
on a speakerphone!

293
00:17:12,615 --> 00:17:14,283
He doesn't even know I walked out.

294
00:17:15,326 --> 00:17:19,830
Why don't we write about
how Gardner Analytics

295
00:17:19,914 --> 00:17:21,499
is buying up television stations

296
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:24,168
and some of the greatest
papers in this country?

297
00:17:25,294 --> 00:17:27,880
"Analytics." Oh, my God.

298
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:31,050
What the fuck does that even mean?

299
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:36,180
According to the autopsy,

300
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,015
natural causes.

301
00:17:38,975 --> 00:17:40,142
Heart attack?

302
00:17:40,226 --> 00:17:42,311
Overdose of his liver medication.

303
00:17:42,895 --> 00:17:44,814
Accidental, presumably.

304
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:50,736
- What aren't you telling me?
- Nothing.

305
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,615
He would never do that intentionally.

306
00:17:55,992 --> 00:17:58,286
Witnesses in the lobby of
the Hay-Adams that night

307
00:17:58,369 --> 00:18:01,080
said the former president
was acting disoriented.

308
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:03,374
Did you share this with his widow?

309
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,376
She's the one who asked
me to look into it.

310
00:18:06,252 --> 00:18:08,129
She suspects the Shepherds.

311
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:10,298
He was with them a lot,
but not that night.

312
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:13,384
- And who was?
- Other than her?

313
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,805
That was her husband, Doug.

314
00:18:19,015 --> 00:18:20,266
She's the president.

315
00:18:21,726 --> 00:18:23,519
Don't you sound devoted, Nathan.

316
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:27,023
My only contact with her is
in my official capacity.

317
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:30,234
Did you think you'd seen the last of me?

318
00:18:32,403 --> 00:18:34,196
That's the last thing I thought.

319
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,242
I'll take that as a compliment.

320
00:18:39,535 --> 00:18:42,496
Doug, here.

321
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:46,679
I tracked his comings and goings back

322
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,680
to when he left the White House.

323
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:52,506
I got my hands on the metadata
going into his computer.

324
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:58,095
LeAnn Harvey's camera phone was
streaming during the crash.

325
00:18:59,639 --> 00:19:02,183
A direct feed to only one IP address.

326
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:03,934
Francis'.

327
00:19:04,018 --> 00:19:05,269
His laptop.

328
00:19:06,812 --> 00:19:08,397
It's not easy to watch, but...

329
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:12,068
- Okay.
- Up to you.

330
00:19:26,624 --> 00:19:27,917
Mr. Hammerschmidt.

331
00:19:29,835 --> 00:19:31,045
Duncan Shepherd.

332
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:34,465
I'm sorry I couldn't be at the
meeting in person this afternoon.

333
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:43,015
My walker drops him off when it's late.

334
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:46,184
Come.

335
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:52,358
You saw my little outburst.

336
00:19:54,527 --> 00:19:55,653
I enjoyed it.

337
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:57,947
The outrage.

338
00:19:58,531 --> 00:19:59,532
We need more of it.

339
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:02,243
I especially liked your appearance
on television the other night.

340
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:04,620
Yeah. Well...

341
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:07,039
I get a little heated sometimes.

342
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:09,750
It's exactly the kind of
exposure the Herald needs.

343
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:13,920
Tom,

344
00:20:13,963 --> 00:20:15,881
you're now part of a conglomerate

345
00:20:15,965 --> 00:20:17,967
with vast influence and reach.

346
00:20:21,971 --> 00:20:25,015
The point is I can bring you
whatever evidence you need.

347
00:20:25,391 --> 00:20:27,560
- Hold on.
- Divorce for pardon.

348
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:30,104
There's a kernel of truth
to it, but your source...

349
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:34,692
And before you say anything,
consider what I'm offering.

350
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:36,736
An opportunity for justice.

351
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:39,780
If you're talking about manufacturing
evidence, Mr. Shepherd,

352
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:42,158
- I'm not interested.
- Beg to differ.

353
00:20:42,450 --> 00:20:44,869
And spare me the seasoned
journalist routine, please.

354
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:46,871
Your 30 years in the business.

355
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:49,457
I've spoken to your old
assistant, Angela.

356
00:20:50,291 --> 00:20:52,126
She's written a piece
about her time with you.

357
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:54,086
I could run it, or...

358
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:59,175
Your dogged pursuit of Frank
Underwood, pardon the pun,

359
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,051
is now your pursuit of his bride.

360
00:21:01,135 --> 00:21:02,136
Hmm.

361
00:21:05,681 --> 00:21:06,724
Think about it.

362
00:21:07,850 --> 00:21:12,313
Men your age, they unravel
very easily these days.

363
00:21:16,317 --> 00:21:18,861
Judge Vincent Abruzzo
has the credentials.

364
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:21,155
The published writings,
the public statements.

365
00:21:21,238 --> 00:21:23,616
It all checks out. Full package.

366
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:26,243
So what's the hesitation, Madam Prez?

367
00:21:26,619 --> 00:21:29,371
Beltway Television is owned
by Gardner Analytics.

368
00:21:29,455 --> 00:21:31,582
It's the latest brainchild
of Duncan Shepherd.

369
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:33,099
So far, I've deflected all questions

370
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:34,709
regarding Ms. Cruz's commentary.

371
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:36,879
Good. Let's not dignify it.

372
00:21:45,513 --> 00:21:47,515
No. That's fine, thank you.

373
00:21:49,183 --> 00:21:52,019
They were a hazard, I couldn't resist.

374
00:21:54,188 --> 00:21:57,149
Sorry I missed the funeral.
Were there psalms?

375
00:21:57,233 --> 00:21:58,818
Number 42.

376
00:21:58,901 --> 00:22:00,444
I love 42.

377
00:22:04,031 --> 00:22:06,700
Nasser had no business
coming to you directly.

378
00:22:08,118 --> 00:22:10,704
Well, I knew if I met with
him, you'd suddenly appear.

379
00:22:11,205 --> 00:22:12,915
He feels lied to, Jane.

380
00:22:13,332 --> 00:22:14,458
Because he was.

381
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:18,170
We were never gonna give those
bandits a seat at the table.

382
00:22:19,213 --> 00:22:21,465
Jane, he's threatened more ICO attacks.

383
00:22:21,549 --> 00:22:24,009
ICO is neutralized, mostly.

384
00:22:24,093 --> 00:22:26,846
It's time to re-think our
involvement in Syria.

385
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:28,389
Stand down, rebuild.

386
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:32,059
This deal is important for all of us.

387
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:33,978
Including the Shepherds.

388
00:22:34,395 --> 00:22:36,355
Look, I'm no fan of that family,

389
00:22:36,981 --> 00:22:40,484
but in the case of Syria,
our interests align.

390
00:22:40,568 --> 00:22:41,986
The next phase of our...

391
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:43,654
presence in the region

392
00:22:44,613 --> 00:22:47,283
is more about the spoils than the peace.

393
00:22:47,658 --> 00:22:49,535
The problem is Petrov,

394
00:22:49,618 --> 00:22:51,537
whom the Shepherds and I despise.

395
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:53,080
What do you have on the Shepherds?

396
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,679
I'm sure one of the several agencies

397
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:58,280
you're involved with has something.

398
00:22:58,294 --> 00:23:00,880
And don't you keep files on
everyone you're dealing with?

399
00:23:01,547 --> 00:23:03,507
Bill and Annette are very careful.

400
00:23:03,591 --> 00:23:05,426
What about Annette's son, Duncan?

401
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:09,763
Well, Mark knows them more than I do.

402
00:23:13,851 --> 00:23:16,896
I thought there were better
options for a former president...

403
00:23:18,647 --> 00:23:20,649
but Annette wouldn't leave Frank alone.

404
00:23:22,526 --> 00:23:24,570
That's their problem, they
don't know when to stop.

405
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:28,319
You know, when you
left three months ago,

406
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:30,320
I wondered where you'd gone.

407
00:23:31,327 --> 00:23:34,705
And then, I didn't think of you at all.

408
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:37,917
You say that.

409
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:41,962
But I detect pain in your
eyes, Madam President.

410
00:23:44,548 --> 00:23:47,426
As a deer longs for streams of water.

411
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:49,887
So I long for you, God.

412
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:52,348
Do you miss him?

413
00:23:54,058 --> 00:23:56,226
God? Always.

414
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:05,110
I'd like you to move in here with
me, Jane, into the White House.

415
00:24:05,736 --> 00:24:06,987
I need your counsel

416
00:24:07,613 --> 00:24:10,407
and your perspective
when it comes to Mark.

417
00:24:13,994 --> 00:24:16,455
The truth is that whole last
year in the White House...

418
00:24:17,998 --> 00:24:19,416
I just lost myself.

419
00:24:21,669 --> 00:24:24,672
And the crazy thing is, I've
never even met Zoe Barnes.

420
00:24:25,547 --> 00:24:27,257
Is that what you told the US Attorney?

421
00:24:27,341 --> 00:24:29,760
Or did you and Claire
Underwood make a deal?

422
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:31,887
The president and I are
on different paths.

423
00:24:33,222 --> 00:24:34,723
You're saying you haven't seen her.

424
00:24:35,432 --> 00:24:36,600
We've spoken.

425
00:24:37,601 --> 00:24:39,812
I just don't see a role for
me in her White House.

426
00:24:42,231 --> 00:24:43,732
I'm working with Congressman Cole.

427
00:24:45,693 --> 00:24:47,319
He's making a play for speaker.

428
00:24:47,403 --> 00:24:48,445
Hmm.

429
00:24:54,076 --> 00:24:55,661
I left the Herald today.

430
00:24:57,913 --> 00:25:00,249
If that's why you wanted to see me,

431
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:02,334
- make a pitch for your new guy.
- No.

432
00:25:03,502 --> 00:25:04,962
No, this is about making amends.

433
00:25:05,379 --> 00:25:06,922
Last fall I started drinking again.

434
00:25:06,980 --> 00:25:08,000
No.

435
00:25:08,010 --> 00:25:11,176
You picked this place because it's
full of bloggers and Hill rats.

436
00:25:11,630 --> 00:25:15,120
Right now, everyone here can
see us talking together,

437
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:16,389
like civilized people.

438
00:25:16,390 --> 00:25:18,851
As if I never called you
a murderer in print.

439
00:25:23,230 --> 00:25:24,690
Your latest article on Francis.

440
00:25:25,482 --> 00:25:27,522
This story about the nights
leading up to his death?

441
00:25:27,568 --> 00:25:28,736
You want to make amends?

442
00:25:29,194 --> 00:25:30,362
Who are your sources?

443
00:25:31,155 --> 00:25:32,239
Peter Russo.

444
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:34,450
Zoe Barnes.

445
00:25:35,034 --> 00:25:36,243
LeAnn Harvey.

446
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:45,294
Doug, there isn't a shadow
for you to hide in anymore.

447
00:25:45,919 --> 00:25:48,338
The only person knows everything is you.

448
00:25:48,922 --> 00:25:49,923
I don't.

449
00:25:52,468 --> 00:25:53,510
Let him go.

450
00:25:58,057 --> 00:25:59,617
I don't know what you're talking about.

451
00:26:03,312 --> 00:26:06,065
At some point, you're
gonna have to decide.

452
00:26:08,442 --> 00:26:11,195
Claire Underwood, believe me,

453
00:26:12,071 --> 00:26:14,114
she'll come for you when it's time.

454
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:17,408
Thanks.

455
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:32,925
You know, there's caffeine in that.

456
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:35,010
I do.

457
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:39,598
I love that you love
Arnold Palmers, but...

458
00:26:40,265 --> 00:26:42,142
Arnold Palmer was a great man.

459
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:46,355
She still on your mind?

460
00:26:51,151 --> 00:26:52,986
This arrangement isn't working.

461
00:26:55,072 --> 00:26:56,365
Which arrangement?

462
00:26:57,491 --> 00:26:58,700
Mark, come to bed.

463
00:27:01,286 --> 00:27:03,956
She needs to feel some
degree of autonomy.

464
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:05,582
Fuck autonomy.

465
00:27:05,666 --> 00:27:07,459
She serves at our pleasure.

466
00:27:07,543 --> 00:27:09,419
I'm sure she feels undervalued.

467
00:27:09,503 --> 00:27:10,629
Undervalued?

468
00:27:10,712 --> 00:27:12,756
Claire Hale? Please.

469
00:27:13,132 --> 00:27:14,412
What if Bill doesn't get better?

470
00:27:18,220 --> 00:27:19,513
He is better.

471
00:27:21,014 --> 00:27:22,432
If we don't play this right,

472
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:24,893
in the public eye, we
are doomed to fail.

473
00:27:24,977 --> 00:27:27,062
- You know that, right?
- She's doomed, you mean.

474
00:27:27,146 --> 00:27:28,897
Look...

475
00:27:30,023 --> 00:27:31,108
Let's be clear.

476
00:27:31,191 --> 00:27:35,112
I am not attracted to her, but she
needs to see me as a partner.

477
00:27:35,195 --> 00:27:37,447
And what is the rush?

478
00:27:38,866 --> 00:27:40,868
Bill wants a majority on the court.

479
00:27:40,951 --> 00:27:42,995
He's waited a long time.

480
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:46,456
Let her at least look
like the president.

481
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:50,127
I'll scuttle the nomination
if it comes to that later.

482
00:27:51,336 --> 00:27:53,714
I want Judge Abruzzo, Mark.

483
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:56,216
And don't ever question
my brother's ability

484
00:27:56,300 --> 00:27:58,385
to function at the highest level.

485
00:28:01,221 --> 00:28:03,182
What is that Sylvia Plath line?

486
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:06,101
"She eats men like air."

487
00:28:06,185 --> 00:28:07,978
Who are we talking about?

488
00:28:17,613 --> 00:28:18,613
Hey.

489
00:28:18,947 --> 00:28:20,532
Sorry we missed each other yesterday.

490
00:28:20,616 --> 00:28:23,702
Well, my apologies for leaving
you in the lurch again today.

491
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:24,828
Everything okay?

492
00:28:24,912 --> 00:28:26,205
I spoke to Annette.

493
00:28:26,288 --> 00:28:28,290
I really think this is the best course.

494
00:28:30,083 --> 00:28:32,502
- Did you ever meet George?
- George?

495
00:28:33,295 --> 00:28:36,465
My brother George. Incurious George.

496
00:28:36,882 --> 00:28:38,300
No, I never did.

497
00:28:38,383 --> 00:28:41,929
And back in the old days, we acquired
an operation in the Midwest,

498
00:28:42,012 --> 00:28:43,764
refining Canadian crude.

499
00:28:43,847 --> 00:28:45,933
Profit margin was...

500
00:28:46,016 --> 00:28:47,684
It was staggering.

501
00:28:47,768 --> 00:28:48,936
But George,

502
00:28:49,019 --> 00:28:51,563
he got all high-minded about it.

503
00:28:52,022 --> 00:28:56,360
Thought that we were bending
too many laws. So he...

504
00:28:56,693 --> 00:29:01,365
He bought a rival company, green
energy type, and he sued us.

505
00:29:02,282 --> 00:29:03,533
Sued us.

506
00:29:04,076 --> 00:29:05,118
I mean...

507
00:29:05,827 --> 00:29:07,079
The betrayal.

508
00:29:08,121 --> 00:29:11,959
My father's true religion was family.

509
00:29:12,542 --> 00:29:13,919
And he was troubled.

510
00:29:14,002 --> 00:29:16,797
He was deeply troubled
by what George had done.

511
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,298
Changed his will.

512
00:29:19,130 --> 00:29:21,399
Any sibling bringing litigation against

513
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:24,020
any other at the time of his death

514
00:29:24,054 --> 00:29:26,598
would automatically lose their
share of the inheritance.

515
00:29:27,057 --> 00:29:28,892
Every damnable penny.

516
00:29:29,977 --> 00:29:31,520
He used that word.

517
00:29:32,312 --> 00:29:34,564
Which is exactly what
happened to George.

518
00:29:35,148 --> 00:29:37,651
Oh. George couldn't believe it.

519
00:29:38,230 --> 00:29:40,999
Accused me of tricking Dad into doing it

520
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:43,340
when he was too weak
to know his own mind.

521
00:29:43,365 --> 00:29:47,035
My father always knew his own mind.

522
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:48,954
George...

523
00:29:50,831 --> 00:29:53,333
... he was just so broken up about it.

524
00:29:55,502 --> 00:29:57,379
Didn't even contest the will.

525
00:29:57,921 --> 00:29:59,089
Which as far as I see it,

526
00:29:59,170 --> 00:30:00,759
it means he had no place inheriting

527
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:02,900
that kind of money to begin with.

528
00:30:03,552 --> 00:30:06,596
The man had everything he ever needed.

529
00:30:07,139 --> 00:30:08,348
He was just so...

530
00:30:09,433 --> 00:30:10,809
Short-sighted.

531
00:30:13,228 --> 00:30:15,522
Lives on some island in Maine now.

532
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:18,400
You know what the worst part for me was?

533
00:30:19,026 --> 00:30:20,944
How much it upset Annette.

534
00:30:22,446 --> 00:30:24,114
That was a no-go.

535
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:27,284
I'll get the nomination, Bill.

536
00:30:28,618 --> 00:30:29,953
Bye-bye now, Mark.

537
00:30:37,710 --> 00:30:39,219
They were good enough to provide me

538
00:30:39,220 --> 00:30:41,220
with a direct feed from the Hall.

539
00:30:46,428 --> 00:30:48,930
- Is this necessary?
- Inhale.

540
00:30:52,434 --> 00:30:54,936
- You ever seen Giselle?
- Mm-mm.

541
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:02,846
Don't look at me like that.

542
00:31:03,612 --> 00:31:05,072
The results aren't all bad.

543
00:31:08,617 --> 00:31:10,243
I'm being watched.

544
00:31:10,619 --> 00:31:11,828
By whom?

545
00:31:12,162 --> 00:31:15,123
Tom Hammerschmidt, the US Attorney.

546
00:31:15,874 --> 00:31:18,168
It's a feeling that
I've had for a while.

547
00:31:20,212 --> 00:31:21,254
Hello?

548
00:31:21,755 --> 00:31:22,756
I'm here.

549
00:31:24,925 --> 00:31:26,176
It's too risky.

550
00:31:27,219 --> 00:31:30,347
If Francis had asked,
you'd have found a way.

551
00:31:32,015 --> 00:31:33,016
That's true.

552
00:31:33,809 --> 00:31:35,310
Well, I'm sorry to hear that.

553
00:31:36,520 --> 00:31:39,022
I guess this is where
we part ways, Doug.

554
00:31:40,232 --> 00:31:41,400
It's for the best.

555
00:31:42,067 --> 00:31:43,318
Then say goodbye.

556
00:31:49,241 --> 00:31:51,284
You know what the last
thing he said to me was?

557
00:31:53,203 --> 00:31:55,831
"I can't imagine a world
with only one of you in it."

558
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:11,263
There comes a point in every
relationship where you wonder,

559
00:32:11,596 --> 00:32:12,764
"Are you with me?"

560
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:16,892
Are you?

561
00:32:18,560 --> 00:32:20,079
So, there are some loose ends

562
00:32:20,080 --> 00:32:21,897
that Bill Shepherd is trying to exploit.

563
00:32:21,898 --> 00:32:23,191
One being...

564
00:32:23,500 --> 00:32:24,520
Cathy Durant.

565
00:32:24,568 --> 00:32:27,612
And I have known each other
for a very long time.

566
00:32:27,696 --> 00:32:28,822
I know.

567
00:32:28,905 --> 00:32:31,867
Well, the last time I saw Cathy,
she looked at death's door.

568
00:32:35,579 --> 00:32:37,247
You can't ask that of me.

569
00:32:38,915 --> 00:32:40,584
She trusts you, Jane.

570
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:43,128
She trusts you.

571
00:32:44,546 --> 00:32:46,923
That's making a move in broad daylight.

572
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:50,552
I enjoy having you here.

573
00:32:55,432 --> 00:32:57,642
I'll never be able to forgive myself.

574
00:33:02,564 --> 00:33:04,441
And when you told him about LeAnn?

575
00:33:04,524 --> 00:33:06,318
He showed no emotion, ma'am.

576
00:33:06,860 --> 00:33:08,987
- Where is he now?
- Still at home.

577
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:11,156
I have a couple of agents trailing him.

578
00:33:11,239 --> 00:33:14,201
As far as the Bureau is concerned,
it's for Doug's own safety.

579
00:33:14,284 --> 00:33:15,284
Hmm.

580
00:33:16,244 --> 00:33:20,123
And besides Congressman Cole,
has he met with anyone?

581
00:33:20,207 --> 00:33:22,876
Other than myself, Tom Hammerschmidt.

582
00:33:26,630 --> 00:33:29,049
Perhaps you should be the one on him.

583
00:33:29,132 --> 00:33:31,885
In case we need to find
him alone at some point.

584
00:33:32,427 --> 00:33:35,263
I continue to be very concerned
about his state of mind.

585
00:33:36,431 --> 00:33:37,431
Yes, ma'am.

586
00:33:42,062 --> 00:33:45,982
Francis left him everything
in his handwritten will.

587
00:33:47,150 --> 00:33:49,069
Am I curious? Yes.

588
00:33:50,070 --> 00:33:53,323
But not enough to wait for Douglas
Stamper to bring me down.

589
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:58,078
Secretary Durant, Ms.
Davis is in the back.

590
00:33:58,161 --> 00:34:01,039
- Where's Sal?
- He's off. My name is Giancarlo.

591
00:34:01,122 --> 00:34:02,499
It's a pleasure to meet you.

592
00:34:03,416 --> 00:34:04,626
Right this way.

593
00:34:07,003 --> 00:34:08,672
- Very slow today.
- Ah.

594
00:34:20,767 --> 00:34:21,767
Please.

595
00:34:38,076 --> 00:34:39,244
I'm sorry.

596
00:34:40,328 --> 00:34:42,247
- Madam Secretary, please.
- I'm sorry, I'm...

597
00:34:42,330 --> 00:34:43,665
Madam Secretary.

598
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:07,522
- Hey.
- Jane, how could you?

599
00:35:07,606 --> 00:35:09,190
How could you do this to me?

600
00:35:09,274 --> 00:35:11,210
- Listen to me, sweetheart.
- No, you listen to me.

601
00:35:11,234 --> 00:35:12,527
Is this Claire?

602
00:35:12,944 --> 00:35:14,613
Are you doing this for her?

603
00:35:14,696 --> 00:35:15,864
Oh, Cathy.

604
00:35:15,947 --> 00:35:18,241
Once the decision is
made, you can't escape.

605
00:35:18,325 --> 00:35:20,660
Maybe it won't happen today, but...

606
00:35:21,494 --> 00:35:22,787
someday,

607
00:35:22,871 --> 00:35:25,040
someday, I'm afraid.

608
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:26,708
I curse you.

609
00:35:27,917 --> 00:35:32,339
I curse you and wish
you a painful death.

610
00:35:32,922 --> 00:35:37,052
Drawn outand excruciating.

611
00:35:37,135 --> 00:35:38,887
I don't want to disappoint you.

612
00:35:39,429 --> 00:35:41,431
That's not how I'm gonna die.

613
00:35:41,931 --> 00:35:43,350
Well, we'll see.

614
00:35:44,225 --> 00:35:45,310
Will we?

615
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:18,259
I've been thinking about the nomination.

616
00:36:21,429 --> 00:36:22,972
You should go with Abruzzo.

617
00:36:31,731 --> 00:36:34,109
We could get beaten up in the midterms

618
00:36:34,526 --> 00:36:36,778
if the wrong signals are sent.

619
00:36:40,990 --> 00:36:42,701
It's the way to be a two-term president.

620
00:36:44,244 --> 00:36:46,413
There's still a lot we can accomplish.

621
00:36:48,832 --> 00:36:50,583
You're such a strange animal.

622
00:36:52,540 --> 00:36:54,159
You've never been
comfortable in your skin

623
00:36:54,160 --> 00:36:56,160
since you've been vice president.

624
00:36:57,298 --> 00:36:58,800
Why did you even try?

625
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:04,723
I believe in you.

626
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:08,518
Well, that's not enough.

627
00:37:11,104 --> 00:37:12,647
I'll leave you to your movie then.

628
00:37:14,691 --> 00:37:16,818
What does Annette have
to say about all this?

629
00:37:19,571 --> 00:37:22,282
- I know you're close to her.
- I won't betray her.

630
00:37:24,743 --> 00:37:26,578
Just like I won't betray you, Claire.

631
00:37:27,287 --> 00:37:28,788
They got us, you know?

632
00:37:47,515 --> 00:37:48,933
We should make the announcement.

633
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:51,728
Abruzzo.

634
00:38:07,118 --> 00:38:08,620
You can start the film.

635
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:54,099
She's already met with the
EPA Regional Administrator,

636
00:38:54,123 --> 00:38:55,583
looking for memos.

637
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,520
Hard disks have been scrubbed, and
there's nothing in the cloud.

638
00:38:58,545 --> 00:39:00,922
There's no paper trail,
virtual or otherwise.

639
00:39:03,216 --> 00:39:06,010
- Skorsky?
- She was with the Herald.

640
00:39:06,094 --> 00:39:07,679
She left when I joined the White House.

641
00:39:07,762 --> 00:39:09,931
It's just a local paper.
We can acquire it.

642
00:39:10,390 --> 00:39:12,392
This isn't about the
president grandstanding.

643
00:39:12,767 --> 00:39:14,394
She's talking to someone.

644
00:39:16,020 --> 00:39:18,314
- Duncan...
- We should save the app for the midterms.

645
00:39:19,148 --> 00:39:21,192
Well, do you trust what
you've built or not?

646
00:39:21,276 --> 00:39:22,485
I don't want it exposed.

647
00:39:22,569 --> 00:39:24,070
She signed up for the app.

648
00:39:24,153 --> 00:39:26,489
We can get into her phone,
take a look around.

649
00:39:28,533 --> 00:39:30,285
Would you gentlemen excuse us?

650
00:39:30,577 --> 00:39:32,871
No, stay. Bill.

651
00:39:40,837 --> 00:39:42,297
She wants to see me.

652
00:39:43,506 --> 00:39:46,301
Uh-uh. Nope.

653
00:39:47,218 --> 00:39:50,388
She says Mark is no longer
a viable vice president.

654
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:52,390
He's not communicating her wishes.

655
00:39:52,974 --> 00:39:55,143
She wants to deal directly with me.

656
00:39:55,852 --> 00:39:58,646
She's in no position to demand anything.

657
00:40:03,818 --> 00:40:04,944
My God.

658
00:40:05,612 --> 00:40:07,196
You want to meet with her.

659
00:40:07,614 --> 00:40:09,407
She's still the president.

660
00:40:10,074 --> 00:40:11,784
Who had three abortions,

661
00:40:12,577 --> 00:40:14,454
lied to the American people about one.

662
00:40:14,537 --> 00:40:16,831
I told you, I'm not willing to use that.

663
00:40:20,335 --> 00:40:21,878
Then you'll use the other thing.

664
00:40:23,838 --> 00:40:25,089
What Mark told us.

665
00:40:27,967 --> 00:40:31,346
Seal. The case was pretty typical.

666
00:40:31,429 --> 00:40:32,847
Prep school drugs.

667
00:40:33,473 --> 00:40:36,976
Duncan Shepherd was rich enough
to get off, but the other boy,

668
00:40:37,352 --> 00:40:38,436
not so lucky.

669
00:40:39,354 --> 00:40:40,354
But...

670
00:40:40,563 --> 00:40:41,648
the transcript.

671
00:40:41,856 --> 00:40:45,902
- Hmm. Fascinating read.
- Painful, really.

672
00:40:49,781 --> 00:40:50,823
Ms. Shepherd's here.

673
00:40:50,907 --> 00:40:52,187
Oh, please send her in.

674
00:40:55,244 --> 00:40:57,080
- Annette.
- Claire.

675
00:40:58,331 --> 00:41:00,208
- Jane.
- Annette.

676
00:41:00,541 --> 00:41:03,711
I'm honored we've graduated
to a first name basis.

677
00:41:03,795 --> 00:41:05,588
Surnames can be a burden.

678
00:41:05,672 --> 00:41:06,839
That's funny.

679
00:41:07,340 --> 00:41:09,008
I've always loved mine.

680
00:41:09,550 --> 00:41:11,844
What about you, Claire?
You gave yours up.

681
00:41:11,928 --> 00:41:12,971
Exactly.

682
00:41:13,429 --> 00:41:15,098
You feel more like an Underwood?

683
00:41:15,848 --> 00:41:18,601
Well, like you said.
Surnames can be a burden.

684
00:41:18,685 --> 00:41:20,895
I like your...

685
00:41:21,604 --> 00:41:22,814
lady quotes.

686
00:41:22,897 --> 00:41:24,107
What is woman?

687
00:41:24,607 --> 00:41:26,234
De Beauvoir question.

688
00:41:26,317 --> 00:41:29,278
That's right. From The Second Sex?
Remember that class, Annette?

689
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:32,031
How strange it was, as a teenager,

690
00:41:32,115 --> 00:41:35,410
to be taught feminism
by a man in French.

691
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:37,036
I hated that book.

692
00:41:37,286 --> 00:41:38,997
Long-winded, for sure.

693
00:41:39,622 --> 00:41:40,999
But you gotta admit.

694
00:41:41,332 --> 00:41:43,126
She was right about everything.

695
00:41:51,884 --> 00:41:52,927
Work with me.

696
00:41:54,804 --> 00:41:57,140
Directly, without a middleman.

697
00:41:57,223 --> 00:41:58,558
What use is Mark,

698
00:41:58,891 --> 00:42:00,268
if he can't be effective?

699
00:42:00,351 --> 00:42:01,811
Mark can be very effective.

700
00:42:01,894 --> 00:42:04,230
Well, but both sides are unhappy.

701
00:42:04,897 --> 00:42:06,107
The Supreme Court.

702
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:07,900
This is a choice

703
00:42:07,984 --> 00:42:10,319
that outlives any presidency.

704
00:42:10,403 --> 00:42:11,612
Exactly.

705
00:42:11,988 --> 00:42:15,283
But also part of what
defines a presidency.

706
00:42:15,366 --> 00:42:16,534
Of course.

707
00:42:17,118 --> 00:42:18,619
So I can't be...

708
00:42:21,039 --> 00:42:23,416
I will consider any informed opinion.

709
00:42:24,167 --> 00:42:26,919
But I... You understand.

710
00:42:28,171 --> 00:42:30,590
The decision has to be mine, Annie.

711
00:42:33,301 --> 00:42:35,136
No one calls me that anymore.

712
00:42:36,429 --> 00:42:38,222
Your son, how old is he now?

713
00:42:41,267 --> 00:42:43,227
Twenty-seven? No...

714
00:42:43,811 --> 00:42:46,773
Twenty-eight. I always seem
to make him a year younger.

715
00:42:46,856 --> 00:42:48,858
He always did look young for his age.

716
00:42:50,109 --> 00:42:51,986
Especially his juvenile mugshot.

717
00:42:52,820 --> 00:42:54,238
Such a baby face.

718
00:42:56,074 --> 00:42:57,575
So, you'll speak to Bill?

719
00:43:00,536 --> 00:43:01,662
I don't need to.

720
00:43:03,581 --> 00:43:05,666
You're the president. You
should do what you want.

721
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:08,544
That's what I keep thinking.

722
00:43:09,796 --> 00:43:11,839
Do you remember how much
fun we used to have,

723
00:43:12,632 --> 00:43:14,550
before we understood the rules?

724
00:44:06,227 --> 00:44:08,271
Look, let's not let it all
break down here, okay?

725
00:44:08,354 --> 00:44:09,480
Correct me if I'm wrong,

726
00:44:09,564 --> 00:44:12,167
but you've never had a foothold
like this in the White House. So...

727
00:44:12,191 --> 00:44:14,569
You want to save her or fuck her?

728
00:44:14,652 --> 00:44:17,655
- Either way, do it on your time.
- Don't make it personal.

729
00:44:18,489 --> 00:44:20,908
Don't insult me.

730
00:44:24,579 --> 00:44:25,705
Shut her down.

731
00:44:26,622 --> 00:44:27,622
Show it to her.

732
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:30,793
That's what Bill and I want.
And you'll do it.

733
00:44:31,127 --> 00:44:32,127
No.

734
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:37,383
- I'm not asking.
- The fallout from that...

735
00:44:37,400 --> 00:44:38,430
Not my concern.

736
00:44:38,467 --> 00:44:40,261
It will be your concern.

737
00:44:47,935 --> 00:44:49,478
You're on your own now.

738
00:44:50,396 --> 00:44:52,940
- Oh, no, no, we're done.
- Don't.

739
00:44:54,692 --> 00:44:55,776
Annette.

740
00:45:00,907 --> 00:45:03,492
The reign of the middle-aged
white man is over.

741
00:45:04,076 --> 00:45:06,579
The Bill Shepherds of the
world who won't let go,

742
00:45:06,662 --> 00:45:07,872
have to go.

743
00:45:08,280 --> 00:45:09,999
The waitress who filmed it works for

744
00:45:10,000 --> 00:45:11,949
the Shepherd Freedom Foundation.

745
00:45:11,950 --> 00:45:13,439
They were hoping to use
the clip when it came to

746
00:45:13,440 --> 00:45:15,220
Judge Abruzzo's confirmation.

747
00:45:16,923 --> 00:45:18,174
Okay, thank you.

748
00:45:19,091 --> 00:45:21,260
Have you heard from Tom Yates, Kelsey?

749
00:45:22,678 --> 00:45:24,096
No. Uh...

750
00:45:24,180 --> 00:45:25,765
You were friendly with him, right?

751
00:45:26,891 --> 00:45:29,477
I haven't heard from Tom in a long time.

752
00:45:30,436 --> 00:45:32,897
And your coworkers, have
they asked about him at all?

753
00:45:32,980 --> 00:45:34,315
Now and then.

754
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:36,025
He used to roam around down there.

755
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:37,610
Everyone liked him.

756
00:45:38,810 --> 00:45:40,459
Well, I had my national security team

757
00:45:40,460 --> 00:45:41,906
look into it. And they tracked him down.

758
00:45:41,907 --> 00:45:44,139
It seems he's been using his credit card

759
00:45:44,140 --> 00:45:46,320
in and around Prague, apparently.

760
00:45:46,327 --> 00:45:47,578
I'm glad to hear it.

761
00:45:48,996 --> 00:45:51,249
No, because I was worried.

762
00:45:51,332 --> 00:45:54,669
We used to talk a lot, and
then it just stopped.

763
00:45:55,920 --> 00:45:58,297
Did you ever read anything
he was working on...

764
00:45:58,381 --> 00:46:01,467
... besides the speeches
he wrote for me?

765
00:46:01,550 --> 00:46:03,177
No, just the early stuff.

766
00:46:04,971 --> 00:46:05,971
Cathy.

767
00:46:06,681 --> 00:46:07,765
Oh, Stan.

768
00:46:09,642 --> 00:46:11,185
Oh, my God.

769
00:46:12,728 --> 00:46:13,729
That's all for now.

770
00:46:15,648 --> 00:46:16,649
When did it happen?

771
00:46:18,234 --> 00:46:19,986
I'm so, so sorry.

772
00:46:21,770 --> 00:46:23,559
No, the last conversation
I had with her,

773
00:46:23,560 --> 00:46:25,560
she was talking about her new job

774
00:46:26,659 --> 00:46:29,412
and what a great opportunity
it was going to be.

775
00:47:24,175 --> 00:47:25,384
Madam President.

776
00:47:26,218 --> 00:47:28,054
Forgive me for calling so late.

777
00:47:29,555 --> 00:47:31,265
I've just been informed...

778
00:47:32,224 --> 00:47:34,185
that Catherine Durant is dead.

779
00:47:36,520 --> 00:47:39,273
It's an embolism, they're saying.
Connected to her fall.

780
00:47:41,901 --> 00:47:45,738
I want to thank you, Doug,
so much for your help.

781
00:47:52,370 --> 00:47:53,621
It's a shame.

782
00:47:55,289 --> 00:47:56,665
It's a terrible shame.

783
00:47:58,334 --> 00:47:59,377
Yes...

784
00:48:00,878 --> 00:48:02,880
a terrible, terrible shame.

785
00:48:04,006 --> 00:48:05,633
She will be missed.

786
00:49:04,316 --> 00:49:05,316
Mark.

787
00:49:05,770 --> 00:49:07,420
Apologies for disturbing your run.

788
